@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-rules`

-- ca-tests-rules.l4
--
-- The other computable rules (sections 3(1), 8, 9, 11, 17, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23(1), 25, 32, 34, 35(1), 41(1) and the Schedule).
-- Expected values written from the text before the module was run.  `#ASSERT REFUSED` where the text names its cases and the case asked about
-- is not one of them.

§ `Sections 3(1), 8(1), 9 and 17: unless a contrary intention appears, or except as mentioned`

#ASSERT `a provision of the Act applies to an enactment unless` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a provision of the Act applies to an enactment unless` TRUE)
#ASSERT `an enactment applies to the whole of Canada unless` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`an enactment applies to the whole of Canada unless` TRUE)
#ASSERT `a provision in a private Act affects a person's rights if` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a provision in a private Act affects a person's rights if` FALSE)
#ASSERT `an enactment binds or affects Her Majesty or Her Majesty's rights or prerogatives if` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an enactment binds or affects Her Majesty or Her Majesty's rights or prerogatives if` FALSE)

§ `Section 8(2): an amending enactment`

-- The amended enactment does not apply to the part: the amending provision applies only if it says so.
#ASSERT `a provision of an amending enactment applies to a part of Canada where` FALSE `and` TRUE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a provision of an amending enactment applies to a part of Canada where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE)
-- The amended enactment applies to the part: subsection (2) is silent and subsection (1) governs.
#ASSERT `a provision of an amending enactment applies to a part of Canada where` TRUE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a provision of an amending enactment applies to a part of Canada where` TRUE `and` FALSE `and` TRUE)

§ `Sections 8(2.1) and 8(2.2): the exclusive economic zone and the continental shelf`

#ASSERT `an enactment applies also to the exclusive economic zone of Canada where` TRUE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`an enactment applies also to the exclusive economic zone of Canada where` TRUE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an enactment applies also to the exclusive economic zone of Canada where` FALSE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT `an enactment applies also to the continental shelf of Canada where` TRUE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`an enactment applies also to the continental shelf of Canada where` TRUE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an enactment applies also to the continental shelf of Canada where` FALSE `and` FALSE)

§ `Section 8.2: civil law terminology in Quebec, common law elsewhere`

#ASSERT `the terminology or meaning adopted, where an enactment contains both civil law and common law terminology, is` TRUE `unless` FALSE EQUALS `the civil law terminology or meaning`
#ASSERT `the terminology or meaning adopted, where an enactment contains both civil law and common law terminology, is` FALSE `unless` FALSE EQUALS `the common law terminology or meaning`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the terminology or meaning adopted, where an enactment contains both civil law and common law terminology, is` TRUE `unless` TRUE)

§ `Section 11: "shall" and "may"`

#ASSERT `the construction of the expression` `shall` EQUALS `imperative`
#ASSERT `the construction of the expression` `may` EQUALS `permissive`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the construction of the expression` `another expression`)

§ `Section 19: administering an oath`

#ASSERT `an oath under an enactment or a rule of the Senate or House of Commons may be administered by` `a person authorized by the enactment or rule to take the evidence` `where` FALSE
#ASSERT `an oath under an enactment or a rule of the Senate or House of Commons may be administered by` `a judge of any court` `where` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an oath under an enactment or a rule of the Senate or House of Commons may be administered by` `a judge of any court` `where` FALSE)
#ASSERT `an oath under an enactment or a rule of the Senate or House of Commons may be administered by` `a notary public` `where` TRUE
#ASSERT `an oath under an enactment or a rule of the Senate or House of Commons may be administered by` `a justice of the peace` `where` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an oath under an enactment or a rule of the Senate or House of Commons may be administered by` `a commissioner for taking affidavits` `where` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an oath under an enactment or a rule of the Senate or House of Commons may be administered by` `any other person` `where` TRUE)
#ASSERT `a power conferred on a justice of the peace to administer an oath or solemn affirmation or to take an affidavit or declaration may be exercised by a person who is a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths if` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power conferred on a justice of the peace to administer an oath or solemn affirmation or to take an affidavit or declaration may be exercised by a person who is a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths if` FALSE)

§ `Section 20: a report laid before Parliament at a session`

#ASSERT NOT (`the Act that requires a report or document to be laid before Parliament requires it to be laid again at a subsequent session if` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the Act that requires a report or document to be laid before Parliament requires it to be laid again at a subsequent session if` FALSE)

§ `Section 21: corporations`

#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to sue and be sued` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to contract and be contracted with by its corporate name` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to have a common seal and to alter or change it at pleasure` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to have perpetual succession` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to acquire and hold personal property for the purposes for which the corporation is established and to alienate that property at pleasure` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power of a majority of the members to bind the others by their acts` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
-- (b): the power over the forms of the name and seal, for a corporation whose name has an English and a French form.
#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to use either the English or the French form of its name or both forms, and to show both forms on its seal or have two seals` `where` TRUE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to use either the English or the French form of its name or both forms, and to show both forms on its seal or have two seals` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE)
-- (d): members who do not contravene are exempt; the text does not say about one who does.
#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `exemption of individual members who do not contravene the provisions of the enactment from personal liability for its debts, obligations or acts` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words establishing a corporation vest it with` `exemption of individual members who do not contravene the provisions of the enactment from personal liability for its debts, obligations or acts` `where` FALSE `and` TRUE `and` FALSE)
-- (3): banking only if expressly conferred.
#ASSERT `words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to carry on the business of banking` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`words establishing a corporation vest it with` `the power to carry on the business of banking` `where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE)

§ `Section 22: majorities and quorum`

-- (1): a majority of more than two persons.
#ASSERT `the smallest number that is a majority of the persons an enactment requires or authorizes to do a thing, when they number` 3 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the smallest number that is a majority of the persons an enactment requires or authorizes to do a thing, when they number` 4 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the smallest number that is a majority of the persons an enactment requires or authorizes to do a thing, when they number` 5 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the smallest number that is a majority of the persons an enactment requires or authorizes to do a thing, when they number` 6 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the smallest number that is a majority of the persons an enactment requires or authorizes to do a thing, when they number` 2)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the smallest number that is a majority of the persons an enactment requires or authorizes to do a thing, when they number` 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the smallest number that is a majority of the persons an enactment requires or authorizes to do a thing, when they number` 3.5)
-- (2)(a)(i): a fixed number of members; at least one-half is a quorum.
#ASSERT `a quorum exists, where the number of members is fixed at` 5 `and the number present is` 3
#ASSERT NOT (`a quorum exists, where the number of members is fixed at` 5 `and the number present is` 2)
#ASSERT `a quorum exists, where the number of members is fixed at` 4 `and the number present is` 2
#ASSERT NOT (`a quorum exists, where the number of members is fixed at` 4 `and the number present is` 1)
#ASSERT `a quorum exists, where the number of members is fixed at` 3 `and the number present is` 2
#ASSERT NOT (`a quorum exists, where the number of members is fixed at` 3 `and the number present is` 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a quorum exists, where the number of members is fixed at` 2 `and the number present is` 2)
-- (2)(a)(ii): a range; at least one-half of the members in office, if that number is within the range.
#ASSERT `a quorum exists, where the members in office number` 7 `and the range runs from` 5 `to` 9 `and the number present is` 4
#ASSERT NOT (`a quorum exists, where the members in office number` 7 `and the range runs from` 5 `to` 9 `and the number present is` 3)
#ASSERT `a quorum exists, where the members in office number` 5 `and the range runs from` 5 `to` 9 `and the number present is` 3
#ASSERT `a quorum exists, where the members in office number` 9 `and the range runs from` 5 `to` 9 `and the number present is` 5
#ASSERT NOT (`a quorum exists, where the members in office number` 9 `and the range runs from` 5 `to` 9 `and the number present is` 4)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a quorum exists, where the members in office number` 4 `and the range runs from` 5 `to` 9 `and the number present is` 4)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a quorum exists, where the members in office number` 10 `and the range runs from` 5 `to` 9 `and the number present is` 10)
-- (2)(b): an act done by a majority of the members present, if they constitute a quorum, is deemed done by the association.
#ASSERT `an act or thing done at a meeting by` 3 `of` 5 `members present is deemed done by the association where` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an act or thing done at a meeting by` 2 `of` 5 `members present is deemed done by the association where` TRUE)
#ASSERT `an act or thing done at a meeting by` 3 `of` 4 `members present is deemed done by the association where` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an act or thing done at a meeting by` 2 `of` 4 `members present is deemed done by the association where` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an act or thing done at a meeting by` 3 `of` 5 `members present is deemed done by the association where` FALSE)
-- (2)(c): a vacancy does not impair the right to act, if the number in office is not less than a quorum.
#ASSERT `a vacancy does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right to act, where` 3 `are in office and a quorum is` 3
#ASSERT `a vacancy does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right to act, where` 5 `are in office and a quorum is` 3
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a vacancy does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right to act, where` 2 `are in office and a quorum is` 3)

§ `Section 23(1): a public officer holds office during pleasure`

#ASSERT `a public officer is deemed appointed to hold office during pleasure only unless` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a public officer is deemed appointed to hold office during pleasure only unless` TRUE)

§ `Section 25(1): a document that is evidence of a fact`

#ASSERT `in judicial proceedings, where an enactment provides that a document is evidence of a fact, and` FALSE `and` FALSE EQUALS `the document is admissible in evidence and the fact is deemed to be established`
#ASSERT `in judicial proceedings, where an enactment provides that a document is evidence of a fact, and` FALSE `and` TRUE EQUALS `the document is admissible in evidence and the fact is not deemed to be established by this subsection, there being evidence to the contrary`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`in judicial proceedings, where an enactment provides that a document is evidence of a fact, and` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`in judicial proceedings, where an enactment provides that a document is evidence of a fact, and` TRUE `and` TRUE)

§ `Section 32: deviations from a prescribed form`

#ASSERT `a deviation from a prescribed form does not invalidate the form used where` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a deviation from a prescribed form does not invalidate the form used where` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a deviation from a prescribed form does not invalidate the form used where` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a deviation from a prescribed form does not invalidate the form used where` TRUE `and` TRUE)

§ `Section 34: offences`

#ASSERT `the class of an offence created by an enactment where` TRUE `and` FALSE EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `the class of an offence created by an enactment where` TRUE `and` TRUE EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `the class of an offence created by an enactment where` FALSE `and` FALSE EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the class of an offence created by an enactment where` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person convicted on summary conviction is considered convicted of an indictable offence by reason only of that conviction where` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a person convicted on summary conviction is considered convicted of an indictable offence by reason only of that conviction where` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the provisions of the Criminal Code that apply to an offence of the class` `an indictable offence` `unless` FALSE EQUALS `the provisions relating to indictable offences`
#ASSERT `the provisions of the Criminal Code that apply to an offence of the class` `an offence punishable on summary conviction` `unless` FALSE EQUALS `the provisions relating to summary conviction offences`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the provisions of the Criminal Code that apply to an offence of the class` `an indictable offence` `unless` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the class an offence is construed to be, where a document relating to criminal law or procedure refers to it and` TRUE EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `the class an offence is construed to be, where a document relating to criminal law or procedure refers to it and` FALSE EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 41(1): a reference to two or more provisions by number`

#ASSERT `a reference from` 3 `to` 7 `includes` 3
#ASSERT `a reference from` 3 `to` 7 `includes` 7
-- A number between the ends is in the reference by its own words, so it is included (pass 1 asserted a refusal for 5; corrected).
#ASSERT `a reference from` 3 `to` 7 `includes` 4
#ASSERT `a reference from` 3 `to` 7 `includes` 5
#ASSERT `a reference from` 3 `to` 7 `includes` 6
-- The section says nothing of a number outside the two ends.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a reference from` 3 `to` 7 `includes` 9)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a reference from` 3 `to` 7 `includes` 2)
-- "from 12 to 16" includes 12 and 16 (the ends) and 13, 14 and 15 (between), and 11 and 17 are outside.
#ASSERT `a reference from` 12 `to` 16 `includes` 12
#ASSERT `a reference from` 12 `to` 16 `includes` 13
#ASSERT `a reference from` 12 `to` 16 `includes` 14
#ASSERT `a reference from` 12 `to` 16 `includes` 15
#ASSERT `a reference from` 12 `to` 16 `includes` 16
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a reference from` 12 `to` 16 `includes` 11)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a reference from` 12 `to` 16 `includes` 17)
-- A reference written with the ends the other way round still includes its two ends (nothing lies between 16 and 12).
#ASSERT `a reference from` 16 `to` 12 `includes` 16
#ASSERT `a reference from` 16 `to` 12 `includes` 12
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a reference from` 16 `to` 12 `includes` 14)

§ `Section 35(1): "corporation" and "security"`

#ASSERT `in an enactment, a corporation is` TRUE `and not` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`in an enactment, a corporation is` TRUE `and not` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`in an enactment, a corporation is` FALSE `and not` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the number of persons sufficient for security or sureties, given any number expressly required, which is` NOTHING EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of persons sufficient for security or sureties, given any number expressly required, which is` (JUST 2) EQUALS 2

§ `The Schedule and section 35(1) "Commonwealth"`

-- Fifty-one lines follow the heading "SCHEDULE (Section 35)" in the text: 447 to 497.
#ASSERT count `the countries named in the schedule` EQUALS 51
#ASSERT `is a country named in the schedule` "Canada"
#ASSERT `is a country named in the schedule` "Antigua and Barbuda"
#ASSERT `is a country named in the schedule` "Western Samoa"
#ASSERT `is a country named in the schedule` "Zimbabwe"
#ASSERT `is a country named in the schedule` "United Kingdom"
#ASSERT `is a country named in the schedule` "St. Christopher and Nevis"
#ASSERT NOT (`is a country named in the schedule` "France")
#ASSERT NOT (`is a country named in the schedule` "United States")
#ASSERT `is a member of the British Commonwealth` "India"
-- Section 35(2): the Governor in Council may add or delete by order.
#ASSERT `is a member of the Commonwealth after orders under section 35(2), if` "France" `has been added` TRUE `or deleted` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`is a member of the Commonwealth after orders under section 35(2), if` "Canada" `has been added` FALSE `or deleted` TRUE)
#ASSERT `is a member of the Commonwealth after orders under section 35(2), if` "Canada" `has been added` FALSE `or deleted` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`is a member of the Commonwealth after orders under section 35(2), if` "France" `has been added` FALSE `or deleted` FALSE)
